WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
[dial-up modem connects]

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:09.434
What if sending money worked like sending a text? Jeremy texts a dollar to Jacob's phone number. That's the whole interface.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:17.959
The operator replies with a one-time code. Without it, nothing moves. Not even an AI agent acting for Jeremy can skip it.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.408
And it's sent. A real transaction on Solana, with test dollars for now.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.544
Meanwhile, in Portugal, Jacob's phone lights up.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.920
[chime] You've got money!

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.865
Here's what a bank transfer won't give you: a public receipt for every payment...

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.758
...and one tap to see it finalized on-chain.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.737
Now Jacob sends it back. Same thing. A text, and a code.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.848
No bank wire. No currency exchange. No waiting days for it to clear.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.150
[chime] You've got MONEY!

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:14.442
No app. No seed phrase. No wallet address. Just a conversation. This is Dial Operator. Dial Up Banking.
